# <type>(<scope>): <short summary in imperative mood>
# |<----                Keep header under 72 characters               ---->|

# Explain WHY this change is being made and any Tiptap / Strapi v5 context:
# |<----                  Wrap body lines at 100 chars                ---->|

# Footer (optional):
# Closes #123
# BREAKING CHANGE: <description of breaking change and migration steps>

# --- COMMIT CONVENTIONS (strapi-plugin-tiptap-editor) ---
# Allowed <type> values:
#   feat     - New Tiptap extension, toolbar control, preset, or serialization mode
#   fix      - Bug fix in editor state, Strapi media library integration, RTL, or a11y
#   docs     - README or configuration documentation update
#   style    - Toolbar/BubbleMenu styling or Strapi Design System v2 theme adjustments
#   refactor - Code restructuring without changing public behavior
#   perf     - Editor rendering, debounce, or bundle size optimization
#   test     - Adding or updating Vitest unit tests (admin or server)
#   build    - @strapi/sdk-plugin build, peerDependencies, or TypeScript config
#   ci       - GitHub Actions workflow or release configuration
#   chore    - Maintenance tasks
#
# Common <scope> values:
#   editor, toolbar, bubble-menu, slash-command, media, tables, callout,
#   rtl, i18n, serializer, presets, server, a11y, types, deps
#
# Examples:
#   feat(slash-command): add keyboard-accessible callout block insertion
#   fix(serializer): preserve empty paragraph nodes in markdown round-trip
